<header><p class="enc-kicker">Person</p><h1 class="enc-title">Dumnacus</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates">1st century BCE</span></p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Dumnacus was a leader of the Andecavi, a Gallic people of the lower <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/loire">Loire</a> around <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/angers">Angers</a>. During the last revolts against <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/julius-caesar">Julius Caesar</a> in 51 BCE he besieged <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/duratius">Duratius</a>, the pro-Roman chief of the Pictones, in <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/poitiers">Lemonum</a> (Poitiers). When Roman forces under Gaius Caninius Rebilus and Gaius Fabius arrived, his army was routed and he fled into the remote parts of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/gaul">Gaul</a>.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/dumnacus.jpg" alt="Dumnacus" width="320" height="160" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: cgb · CC BY-SA 3.0 · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Stat%C3%A8re_d%E2%80%99%C3%A9lectrum_%E2%80%9Caux_aigrettes%E2%80%9D_frapp%C3%A9_par_les_And%C3%A9caves_(r%C3%A9gion_d%27Angers).jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
